# 04 — Nucleosome Sensitivity Analysis

This section covers the classification of nucleosomes as Sensitive, Neutral, or Resistant to MNase digestion from DANPOS3 output, downstream assignment of gene names, occupancy and repositioning analysis, upset plot generation, and figure generation. All R scripts were run in R 4.5.2.

---

## Overview of steps

1. Nucleosome position calling (DANPOS3) — light vs heavy digest
2. BigWig generation and log2 ratio computation (deepTools)
3. Heatmap and k-means clustering (deepTools)
4. Sensitivity classification from DANPOS output (R)
5. Gene name assignment (bedtools)
6. Occupancy, repositioning, and fuzziness analysis (R)
7. Upset plots for cross-condition comparisons (R)
8. Sensitivity proportion figures (R)

---

## Samples

Sensitivity analysis was performed for four conditions, each with two biological replicates:

| Condition | Replicates |
| --- | --- |
| shScramble | rep1, rep2 |
| shHP1α | rep1, rep2 |
| shHP1β | rep1, rep2 |
| shH2AZ | rep1, rep2 |

