## Step 2 — BigWig generation and log2 ratio

DANPOS `.wig` output files were converted to BigWig format using wigToBigWig from the UCSC kentUtils suite:

```bash
./wigToBigWig name_of_file.wig hs1.chrom.sizes name_of_output_file.bw
```

Log2 ratio of light to heavy digest signal was computed using deepTools bigwigCompare to generate MNase sensitivity tracks for genome browser visualization and matrix generation:

```bash
bigwigCompare \
    --binSize 1 \
    --outFileName output_sensitivity.bw \
    --outFileFormat bigwig \
    --bigwig1 light_digest.bw \
    --bigwig2 heavy_digest.bw \
    --skipZeroOverZero \
    --operation log2 \
    --skipNonCoveredRegions
```

Multiple BigWig files can be compared for quality control using multiBigwigSummary and plotCorrelation:

```bash
multiBigwigSummary bins -b file1.bw file2.bw -o multibw.npz

plotCorrelation \
    --corData multibw.npz \
    --corMethod spearman \
    -p heatmap \
    --plotFile correlation_heatmap.png
```

