## Step 3 — Heatmap and k-means clustering

Nucleosome sensitivity bigWig tracks were clustered across all conditions using deepTools computeMatrix and plotHeatmap. K-means clustering (k=7) was performed using the shScramble samples as the reference (`--clusterUsingSamples 1`), and the same cluster order was applied to all other conditions.

```bash
# Compute matrix centered on TSS ±1 kb
computeMatrix reference-point \
    --referencePoint center \
    -b 1000 -a 1000 \
    -R /home/jbenoit/index/T2T_TSS_1kb_reduced_clean.bed \
    -S file1.bw file2.bw \
    -o out.gz \
    -p 30 \
    --missingDataAsZero

# Plot heatmap with k-means clustering (k=7)
plotHeatmap \
    -m out.gz \
    --outFileName out.png \
    --colorList blue,white,gold \
    --legendLocation none \
    --heatmapWidth 10 \
    --plotType se \
    --sortRegions keep \
    --kmeans 7 \
    --clusterUsingSamples 1
```

The cluster assignments output by `plotHeatmap` are saved in `HP1_HPTM_2kb_sen_matrix_og_sort_k7.bed` and used for GO enrichment analysis (Section 07).

