## Step 4 — Sensitivity classification (R)

DANPOS output was filtered and classified into Sensitive, Neutral, and Resistant categories. The `smt_diff_log10pval` column is on a ×10 internal DANPOS scale; divide by 10 before applying thresholds.

```r
library(ggplot2)
library(ggrepel)

setwd("/home/pathtofile/")
df <- read.delim("Your_file_TSS_downsampled.positions.integrative.xls",
                 header = TRUE)

# Step 1: Restrict by FDR
test1_df <- df[df$smt_diff_FDR < 0.01, ]

# Step 2: Restrict by summit location
# Nucleosomes must be within 50 bp of each other to count as the same position
test_df <- test1_df[test1_df$treat2control_dis < 50, ]

# Step 3: Scale log10 p-value to standard units
test_df$smt_diff_log10pval_new <- test_df$smt_diff_log10pval / 10

# Step 4: Define cutoffs
log2FC_cutoff    <- 1.0    # log2 fold change threshold
log10pval_cutoff <- -1.5   # -log10(p) threshold (equivalent to p ~ 0.03)

# Step 5: Classify nucleosomes
test_df$sensitivity <- ifelse(
    test_df$smt_diff_log10pval_new < log10pval_cutoff &
    test_df$smt_log2FC > log2FC_cutoff,
    "Sensitive",
    ifelse(
        test_df$smt_diff_log10pval_new < log10pval_cutoff &
        test_df$smt_log2FC < -log2FC_cutoff,
        "Resistant",
        "Neutral"
    )
)

# Report counts
sensitivity_counts <- table(test_df$sensitivity)
sensitivity_counts["Sensitive"]
sensitivity_counts["Resistant"]
sensitivity_counts["Neutral"]

# Export: chr, start, end, sensitivity category (columns 1, 2, 3, 25)
selected_columns <- test_df[, c(1, 2, 3, 25)]
write.table(selected_columns,
            file = "sample_sensitivity_overview.txt",
            row.names = FALSE, col.names = TRUE,
            sep = "\t", quote = FALSE)

# Optional: volcano plot
ggplot(data = test_df,
       aes(x = smt_log2FC, y = abs(smt_diff_log10pval_new), col = sensitivity)) +
    geom_point(size = 1, alpha = 0.2) +
    geom_hline(yintercept = abs(log10pval_cutoff),
               linetype = "dashed", color = "black", linewidth = 1) +
    geom_vline(xintercept = c(log2FC_cutoff, -log2FC_cutoff),
               linetype = "dashed", color = "black", linewidth = 1) +
    scale_color_manual(values = c("Neutral"   = "light gray",
                                  "Resistant" = "navyblue",
                                  "Sensitive" = "gold")) +
    labs(x = "log2 fold change", y = "-log10 p-value") +
    ylim(c(0, 30)) + xlim(c(-7, 7)) +
    theme_classic(base_size = 15)

ggsave("sample_volcano_plot.png")
```

**Classification cutoffs (applied identically to all four conditions):**

| Parameter | Value | Column |
| --- | --- | --- |
| FDR | \< 0.01 | `smt_diff_FDR` |
| Summit distance | \< 50 bp | `treat2control_dis` |
| log2FC (sensitive) | > 1.0 | `smt_log2FC` |
| log2FC (resistant) | \< −1.0 | `smt_log2FC` |
| −log10(p-value) | > 1.5 | `smt_diff_log10pval / 10` |

This script was run independently for each replicate of each condition, producing `*_sensitivity_overview.txt` files used in downstream steps.

