## Step 5 — Gene name assignment (bedtools)

Sensitivity classification files were intersected with the TSS reference to assign gene names to each nucleosome. The `-f 0.8` flag requires 80% of the nucleosome window to overlap the TSS region.

```bash
for i in *_sensitivity_overview.txt; do
    bedtools intersect \
        -a "$i" \
        -b /home/jbenoit/index/T2T_TSS_1kb_reduced_clean.bed \
        -f 0.8 \
        -wa -wb \
        > "TSS_${i}"
done
```

Output files carry gene name annotations alongside nucleosome coordinates and sensitivity classifications.

