## Step 6 — Occupancy, repositioning, and fuzziness analysis (R)

Changes in nucleosome occupancy, positioning, and fuzziness between conditions were extracted directly from DANPOS `.positions.integrative.xls` output:

```r
setwd("/home/your_file_location")
df <- read.delim("sample_TSS.positions.integrative.xls", header = TRUE)

# Repositioning: summit shift > 50 bp between conditions
reposition_df <- df[df$treat2control_dis > 50, ]

# Increased occupancy: log2FC > 5, p < 0.05, FDR < 0.05
occupancy_up_df <- df[
    df$smt_log2FC > 5 &
    df$smt_diff_log10pval < -1.5 &
    df$smt_diff_FDR < 0.05, ]

# Decreased occupancy: log2FC < -5, p < 0.05, FDR < 0.05
occupancy_down_df <- df[
    df$smt_log2FC < -5 &
    df$smt_diff_log10pval < -1.5 &
    df$smt_diff_FDR < 0.05, ]

# Fuzziness changes: |log2FC| > 1.5, p < 0.05, FDR < 0.05
fuzziness_df <- df[
    (df$fuzziness_log2FC > 1.5 | df$fuzziness_log2FC < -1.5) &
    df$fuzziness_diff_log10pval < -1.5 &
    df$fuzziness_diff_FDR < 0.05, ]

# Export BED files (chr, start, end only)
write.table(reposition_df[, 1:3],
            file = "sample_repositioning.bed",
            sep = "\t", row.names = FALSE, col.names = FALSE, quote = FALSE)
write.table(occupancy_up_df[, 1:3],
            file = "sample_occupancy_increase.bed",
            sep = "\t", row.names = FALSE, col.names = FALSE, quote = FALSE)
write.table(occupancy_down_df[, 1:3],
            file = "sample_occupancy_decrease.bed",
            sep = "\t", row.names = FALSE, col.names = FALSE, quote = FALSE)
write.table(fuzziness_df[, 1:3],
            file = "sample_fuzziness.bed",
            sep = "\t", row.names = FALSE, col.names = FALSE, quote = FALSE)
```

Gene names were assigned to each output BED file using the same bedtools intersect approach as Step 5. Reproducible nucleosome changes were identified as those present across both replicates per condition.

